cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RVCalPy in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "RVCalPy: Radial Velocity from Stellar Spectra (CCF and Broadening Function methods)"
abstract: >-
  RVCalPy is a single-file Python tool that measures the radial velocity of a
  star by comparing an observed spectrum with a template. It implements a
  weighted line-mask cross-correlation function (Baranne et al. 1996; Pepe et
  al. 2002; Pino et al. 2018) and the Rucinski (1992, 2002) Broadening
  Function solved via SVD, with rotational-profile fitting for close binaries,
  a two-stage RV search, barycentric correction from observatory coordinates,
  and built-in spectrograph and observatory registries.
type: software
authors:
